Since no-one has replied for a while, I'll tell you what I know...

I believe this is the latest NT firmware screen (once in F2 setup).  Alpha's
have two ways to display the firmware information:
        menu system (typically for Windows NT systems)
        >>>    (the console prompt for UNIX/VMS)
 Somewhere in the menu system is an option that says to switch the firmware
to use the Console prompt or UNIX/VMS firmware screen (or something
similar).
The next hard reboot will then switch it to console mode (>>>).

If this is an EISA system, you may be need to run EISA configuration
diskette (ECU), just boot from it and save the settings. This is because
EISA settings must be changed if switching between Windows NT and UNIX/VMS.
The floppy may also allow you to select the firmware display mode.

Regards,

Toby


