Subject: Re: Switching between simplex and duplex on a remote printer
Date: 1997/09/26
Message-ID: <342B932F.6022@mat.unimi.it>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 275705003
Organization: Dip. di Matematica - Univ. Studi Milano
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Thanks to Juergen Schroeder for his advice. But we found a better
solution without writing filters. That is yup, a free software by 
Malcolm Herbert. We have an alias like this:
alias lpr1f 'yup -DIBNn 1 \!:2* | lpr \!^' # lpr one face
In this way the command
lpr1f -Pprinter filename
prints in simplex mode without headings, borders, page numbering
on any HP printer with duplex unit.

