How 'bout posting an entry for the others to pick apart.  Note that the uerf
command won't display everything you need to know.  You need to get DECevent
(www.service.digital.com/decevent) to properly display these entries.

If, after installing DECevent and using it to display your error log entries,
you still can't figure it out, post an entry.  Or, if you have maintenance on
your system, have your maintenance organization handle it; you're paying them
to do it!  

Not very likely the controller is the cause of the BBR; the controller just
logged the fact that the drive requested the BBR.  

