> > In your printcap file set  :rp=text
> 
> works for text files only
> 
> :rp=raw
> 
> works for text and postscript
> 
> > As Michael Stenberg suggested (see Unix FAQ), this works
> > for text and postscript files.
> >
> > Marzia Bonecchi
> > Dipartimento di Matematica
> > Universia` di Milano

Sorry, Joe, but rp=text does actually work for text and postscript.
We had the same problem as Daniel with two HP network printers (LaserJet
5M 
and DeskJet 1600CM); rp=printername or rp=raw didn't work for ASCII
files.
We set rp=text and solved the problem. (We did so in Digital Unix and
even in VMS UCX.)
The reason is that LPD daemon adds a CR at the end of each line for a
queue with rp=text, before sending it to the printer; it doesn't do this
if
rp is set raw (this setting works for PCL or Postscript files).

                 Marzia



