Chan Shih-Ping wrote:
> 
> Can anyone explain what the routines in libmach.so do for
> threaded programs. Compiling with cc -pthread pulls
> in libpthread.so as well as libmach.so and libexc.so

Those are libraries required for the threading environment.

> I guess libexc.so is for exceptions but what about
> the stuff in libmach.so (the mach kernel??) like
> thread_create etc.

In particular, yes, libexc provides the standard mechanism for dealing
with exceptions. For a lot of reasons, (including, for example, smooth
integration with languages like Ada and C++ that support exceptions),
POSIX cancellation and pthread_exit are implemented using the native
exception mechanism.

libmach provides the interfaces to the Mach kernel functions. We use
them to create and control kernel threads. In the future we'll be
dropping libmach, as we replace the general Mach interfaces with new
interfaces more specific to our needs -- but of course it won't hurt to
include libmach anyway.

