KATHY.WEST@US.GASES.BOC.COM wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> 
> I am using grep to search many large log files for different events.
> For each line that's matched, I would like to show the matched line and
> the line that immediately follows it.

You could to this with a small awk program.  For example, if you are 
looking for the regular expression "regexp", and want to see the following
line as well, this awk program would do the job:

     awk '/regexp/ {print;c=1;next}; c == 1 {print;c=0}'  inputfiles

This could be extended to print additional lines of following context by
incrementing the variable "c" and then testing against some limit before
resetting to 0.

