The real fault is in cron. The code from OSF (originally from AIX)
contains several dereferences of a pointer which may have not been
defined yet. If such a an event happens cron seg faults and dies. The
dump command just happens to produce this behaviour. The fixes to cron
were incorporated in a later release (V3.mumble).

