Jon Erdman <jxe4511*nospam*@rit.edu> writes:
>anyone know how to get the floppy drive working on an alphaserver
>1000A? a man -k floppy only comes up with fd, which creates a bunch
>of character special files in /dev/fd. 
>
>apparently, sec can format floppies, and mtools can copy, read, etc
>DOS files. i have all this info, but i can't mung it all together to
>figure out what order to do things in to get it to work.

I haven't used mtools on DUNIX, but I have on Ultrix and the following does
work there so ...

mtools want to talk to a character special device call /dev/PC_floppy. 
First you must find where the real flopy drive is.  DECstation had the
floppy hanging off of the SCSI bus and it could be identified with 'file
/dev/rrz*c'.  On AlphaServers try file '/dev/rfd0a'.  Use the 'ls -ld
/dev/rfd0a' to get the major and minor device numbers.  Then use 'mknod
/dev/PC_floppy c major# minor#' to make the character special file.  Double
check it with 'ls -ld /dev/PC_floppy'.

This **SHOULD** be all that mtools wants.  As I said, works on Ultrix ...


