Message-ID: <342646FD.41C6@dcs.rhbnc.ac.uk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 274612338
Organization: Royal Holloway College, University of London
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Just to warn you of a nasty security gotcha I found when upgrading from
Digital Unix 3.2C to 4.0B: all the tape devices became world readable
and writable. So if we hadn't fixed it any user could have read our dump
tapes.

Easy to fix; just type 
	chmod o-rw /dev/*mt*
Bob
