X-Deja-AN: 274847261
Organization: Royal Holloway College, University of London
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Some time ago someone asked about Xdec processes burning up CPU time on
Digital Unix. Well, it appears that on DU 4.0B this happens whenever you
put a font server in the font path.

This can happen without you realising it if you use products such as
NCD's Wincenter.

If it does happen you can cure it by sending a HUP signal to the Xdec
process. This will reset the X server (and hence logout the console
user).

Bob
