of digging around in DU manuals showed me that I needed to recompile 
the kernel with an entry for the new device.  The man page for doconfig
gives more instructions on how to do this.

If you'd like to test before trying to build a new kernel, boot up the
machine with the generic kernel (genvmunix) that should be in your 
root directory.  You should be able to boot the generic kernel from
the bootup prompt with:

>>> boot -fi genvmunix

The generic kernel has support for all standard devices in it.  Thus, if 
you boot up with it, your new device should show up.  Watch the messages
produced as you boot with it to see if it shows up.

If it does, you should run doconfig while you're running with the generic
kernel -- if you do doconfig with your old kernel, it may not see the new
device.

--
Travis Casey
casey_t@dep.state.fl.us



