John Wang (rwang@erols.com) wrote:
: Hi, all:

:    I have a DEC 3000 running DEC UNIX 3.2c.  I installed OS and Oracle. 
: Everything is cool except this annoying thing.  If I log into the Oracle
: account, when I do su, I keep getting "I do not have permission".  what is
: happening here?? 

If you want to su to root, then the issuing username must be in 
group 0 (system).  I.e. you need to add the Oracle account name to group
system in /etc/group.

:    Also I noticed that I can only login as root from the server itself.  If
: I login as root through telnet, it will say root cannot login from this
: terminal.  Is there any way I can avoid this??

You will need to add this line:

ptys

to the /etc/securettys file, to allow root logins from pseudoterminals.
(This is not allowed by default as it is a potential security risk:  Root's
password will be passed over your network.)


