product. In this caso you don't have any problem, you need only to
export in NFS your NT file system and to mount with a "mount -t NFS
xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx:/directory_path /mount-path" on your Linux box.
Istead of, if you haven't any NFS products, you can mount a SMB export
of your NT box installing SMB-tools on your Linux machine and compiling
the kernel of your Linux PC with SMB support.
