: and duplex unit.
: We cannot do as with the other printer, because DCPS doesn't support
: network printers; moreover under Unix we'd prefer a solution not VMS
: based.
: Both under VMS and under Digital Unix we define the queue as a remote
: queue with rm=laser_ps2 (the printer itself) and rp=text.
: Under VMS we do this using UCX.
: In this way we can print ASCII and PostScript files but only in
: duplex mode. The above commands to obtain simplex printing don't

For ps on a HP-LJ*4*SI*MX write two little filters which places  one  of
these early in the PostScript file:

        statusdict begin true/false setduplexmode end

   or (maybe, this is untested!)

        statusdict begin    
                /setduplexmode known {true/false setduplexmode} 
        end 

Under unix you can use these filters as "of" in the printcap and set  up
two queues.

Juergen



