> 
> Hi all,
> 	I have an application running on DU 4.0b , which has a
> number of forked child processes. However , if I kill this application
> , the children get orphaned off to PID 1 (The normal behaviour). I 
> was wondering if any signal is given to the child by the parent or
> if there was any way of detecting this on the child side so I could
> destruct it cleanly.  Any help would be greatly appreciated.
> 				TIA
> 					Billy

The easiest method is to check the parent process id, if it is 1 then init
has become the parent. 

The call looks something like this

    ppid = getppid();

There are a couple of other ways to do it using semaphores that are more
complicated.




