Avoid file striping of your root file system.  If you have a database
with several key files that are rather large (i.e. >1gig) striping will
get you much faster throughput. We are striping most of the key database
files for our OLTP system. The downside is that you have increased your
risk exposure across multiple drives, meaning that the probability of a
hardware failure affecting the striped files increases. However, most
database will be effectively crippled anyway in the event of a disk
failure, even if the disk does not contain the major files.  hope this
helps.

