> I have a 2100 4/275.
> What is SCSI CAM
> Does it neccessary for configuring SCSI Devices?
> 
SCSI CAM is the device driver for SCSI devices, the Common Access Method
(I think). It is used when configuring SCSI devices for communicating
with the devices.

With Digital Unix 4.0, it is used by the scu (SCSI Configuration
Utility) and scsimgr utilities, for automatically configuring SCSI
devices on reboot, without the need for rebuilding the kernel.

